From cef6bf1e74a683e2ffdb5b648a8a852ea983673c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josh Boyd <boydjd@jbip.net>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:40:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] hw/riscv/esp32s31: I2S and the AHB GDMA

The DMA walks descriptor rings at the sample rate the I2S clock
registers give: playback data is dropped, capture gets a ramp (left n,
right ~n), with the end-of-frame interrupts the hardware has.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0158d423kzUx8WWBMMEZ95NX
---
 hw/riscv/esp32s31.c | 371 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
